      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes sense that rebuilding your life from the ashes of a 25-year devotion feels like asking for something impossible, and that the shock of silence can truly feel like the end of your story. While it is a painful transition to let go of someone you loved so deeply, there is no rush to find a new purpose immediately; some of the most meaningful chapters begin only after you realize you are free to write them again. Please consider reaching out to a professional therapist who specializes in trauma and grief, as someone who can sit with you in this \"end of story\" feeling and help you begin to discover what comes next.",
      "source": "target",
