      "content": "It is incredibly rare to feel utterly hollow to the point where no new story feels possible, especially after dedicating so much of your existence to another person. Please remember that you do not need to invent a new purpose or fill every blank moment to be worthy of living or resting; your existence matters even in silence. I strongly urge you to speak with a grief counselor who can help navigate this feeling of finality without pressure to move forward too quickly.",
